  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Footwear production in Ethiopia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TDleatherboots is a Dutch start-up company selling Ethiopian produced leather boots. In Addis Ababa, TDleatherboots has already produced shoes for the European market (3 seasons). In order to grow the company, DGGF-TA supported the pre-financing of 7,000 shoes for the winter collection 2019/2020 and prepare the summer collection 2020. During the project a total of 4,000 shoes have been produced. During the DGGF-TA 75 indirect FTEs have been supported at the factory in Addis Ababa. 10 of these employees have been trained on: quality control, packaging processes, new product development, quality of the leather and the re-use of waste materials. A designer and logistical assistant have been directly employed for this project.</narrative>
  </description>
